 "おだい": "تُهْمَة (accusation) / اِتَّهَمَ (To formally accuse (a person) of a crime.) / شَحَنَ (To place a burden, load or responsibility on or in.) / شَحَنَ (To load equipment with material required for its use, as a firearm with powder, ) / هَاجَمَ (To move forward quickly and forcefully, particularly in combat and/or on horseba)  [charge (for admission, a meal, etc.)]",
 "おだいじに": "أَتَمَنَّى لَكَ الشِّفَاءَ الْكَامِل, أَتَمَنَّى لَكِ الشِّفَاءَ الْكَامِل (Expressing hope that the listener will soon recover from illness.)  [get well soon]\nمثال: くれぐれもお体をお大事に。\n→ Please take good care of yourself.",
 "おだいばん": "سُفْرَة (A table, usually in a dining room or dining hall, on which meals are served.)  [dining table] / [cooked rice]\nsecret language of court ladies",
 "おだいもく": "[Nichiren chant] / شِعَار (A catchphrase associated with a product or service being advertised.)  [(an empty) slogan]",
 "おだく": "تَلْوِيث, تَلَوُّث (Physical contamination, now especially the contamination of the environment by h)  [pollution]",
 "おだちん": "مُكَافَأَة, ثَوَاب (Something of value given in return for an act.) / جَائِزَة (A prize promised for a certain deed or catch) / جَزَاء (The result of an action, whether good or bad.) / مَنَحَ (To give a reward to or for.)  [reward]",
 "おだてる": "تَمَلَّقَ, تَبَصْبَصَ (To compliment someone, often (but not necessarily) insincerely and sometimes to )  [to flatter]\nمثال: まず彼をおだてておいたほうがいいですよ。\n→ You had better try buttering him up first.",
 "おだやか": "هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm]\nمثال: 海は穏やかに、そしてなめらかに見える。\n→ The sea looks calm and smooth. / مُعْتَدِل (Not excessive; acting in moderation.)  [moderate]",
 "おだんごあたま": "كَعْكَة (a small bread roll, often sweetened or spiced)  [bun (hairstyle)]",
 "おだんごヘア": "كَعْكَة (a small bread roll, often sweetened or spiced)  [bun (hairstyle)]",
 "おち": "اِنْزَلَقَ (To lose one’s traction on a slippery surface; to slide due to a lack of friction)  [slip] / نَتِيجَة (The scoreline; the result.)  [outcome]\nمثال: そんなにがぶがぶ飲み続けると、アル中になるのがオチですよ。\n→ If you go on drinking so much, you may well end up an alcoholic. / نُكْتَة (The final part of a joke; the word, sentence, or exchange of sentences that is i)  [punch line (of a joke)]\noften オチ\nمثال: オチの意味がわからなかったらすいません・・・。\n→ If you don't get the punch line, I'm sorry.",
 "おちあう": "[to meet up (as arranged) ; to rendezvous]\nمثال: 君の家と私の家の中間で落ち合うことにしよう。\n→ Let's meet halfway between your house and mine. / وَصَلَ (To connect or combine into one; to put together.) / اِتَّصَلَ (To come together; to meet.) / اِلْتَحَقَ بِـ, اِنْضَمَّ إِلَى (To become a member of.)  [to join (of roads, rivers, etc.)]",
 "おちいりやすい": "مناسب (Suitable; appropriate; fit or fitted; suited.)  [apt (to)]",
 "おちいる": "[to fall into (e.g. a hole)]\nمثال: これが原因でたいていの街の浴場は困難な状態に陥った。\n→ This caused most of the local bath-houses to fall on hard times. / [to fall into (chaos, depression, dilemma, illness, etc.)] / [to fall into (a trap, etc.)] / وَقَعَ, سَقَطَ (To be moved downwards.) / سَقَطَ (To happen; to come to pass; to chance or light (upon).) / سُقُوط, هُوِيّ (The act of moving to a lower position under the effect of gravity.)  [to fall]",
 "おちおち": "بِهُدُوء (Producing little or no noise.)  [quietly]\nمثال: 子供の学費を考えると、おちおちビールも飲んでられないな。\n→ Knowing how much school for my kids is costing, it's impossible to relax with a beer and take it easy.",
