 "おちついた": "هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm] / اِسْتَعْمَرَ (to fix one's dwelling) / اِسْتَوْطَنَ (to fix one's dwelling) / اِسْتَقَرَّ (to fix one's dwelling)  [settled] / صَامِت, هَادِئ (With little or no sound; free of disturbing noise.)  [quiet]",
 "おちつき": "هُدُوء (The state of being calm; tranquillity; silence.)  [calmness]\nمثال: 彼は心の落ち着きを失った。\n→ His presence of mind deserted him. / اِسْتِقْرَار (The condition of being stable or in equilibrium, and thus resistant to change.)  [stability]",
 "おちつく": "أَهْدَأَ, هَدَّأَ (To become less excited, intense, or angry.) / أَهْدَأَ, هَدَّأَ (To cause to become less excited, intense, or angry.)  [to calm down]\nمثال: 彼は当惑して落ち着きませんでした。\n→ He felt lost and uncomfortable. / أَهْدَأَ, هَدَّأَ (To become less excited, intense, or angry.) / أَهْدَأَ, هَدَّأَ (To cause to become less excited, intense, or angry.)  [to calm down] / هَدَأَ (To make or become quiet and calm after a period of disturbance or restlessness.) / اِسْتَقَرَّ (To establish a settled lifestyle for oneself, especially by marrying.)  [to settle down (in a location, job, etc.)] / [to be settled (of an arrangement, conclusion, etc.) ; to be fixed]",
