 "おねいさん": "الْأُخْت الْكُبْرَى, الشَّقِيقَة الْكُبْرَى (Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see older, sister. (This entry is)  [older sister]\nusu. お姉さん\nمثال: あなたのお姉さんは審美感があるね。\n→ Your sister has a sense of beauty. / [young lady]\nvocative / أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [miss]\nreferring to a waitress, etc.; usu. お姐さん / [ma'am]\nused by geisha to refer to their superiors; usu. お姐さん",
 "おねうち": "صَفْقَة (An agreement between parties concerning the sale of property; or a contract by w)  [bargain]",
 "おねえさん": "الْأُخْت الْكُبْرَى, الشَّقِيقَة الْكُبْرَى (Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see older, sister. (This entry is)  [older sister]\nusu. お姉さん\nمثال: あなたのお姉さんは審美感があるね。\n→ Your sister has a sense of beauty. / [young lady]\nvocative / أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [miss]\nreferring to a waitress, etc.; usu. お姐さん / [ma'am]\nused by geisha to refer to their superiors; usu. お姐さん",
 "おねえちゃん": "الْأُخْت الْكُبْرَى, الشَّقِيقَة الْكُبْرَى (Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see older, sister. (This entry is)  [older sister]\nمثال: 私はお姉ちゃんの夕飯をラップに包んでしまわないと。\n→ I have to wrap my sister's dinner in cling film. / صبية (girl — see also girl)  [lass]\nمثال: ママ〜！あのお姉ちゃんとお兄ちゃん、お手手繋いで、すっごく仲良しさんだね〜！\n→ Mama! That lady and man are holding hands, they're great friends aren't they!",
 "おねがい": "طَلَبَ (to express the need or desire for) / طَلَب, مَسْأَلَة (Act of requesting (with the adposition at in the presence of possessives, and on)  [request]\nمثال: 「スミスさんをお願いしたいのですが」「スミスですが」\n→ \"I'd like to talk to Mr Smith.\" \"This is Smith speaking.\" / أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: 頼みたいことがあります。ちょっとお願いしてもよろしいでしょうか？\n→ I need a favor.",
 "おねがいいたします": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: お願いいたします、最後までお聞きください。\n→ I do beseech you, hear me through.",
 "おねがいごと": "طَلَبَ (to express the need or desire for) / طَلَب, مَسْأَلَة (Act of requesting (with the adposition at in the presence of possessives, and on)  [request]\nمثال: あなたにお願い事をしてもよいでしょうか。\n→ Can I ask you a favor?",
 "おねがいします": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: フライトの再確認をお願いします。\n→ Flight reconfirmation, please.",
 "おねがいだから": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: お願いだから泣かないで。\n→ Please don't cry.",
 "おねがいもうしあげる": "سَأَلَ, سأل (To request or petition.)  [to ask (humbly)]\nمثال: 浅学非才の私ではありますが、何とぞ皆様のお力を賜りたく、ここにお願い申し上げる次第です。\n→ I may not have much to offer in the way of learning or ability, but I want to do whatever I can for us all and humbly ask for your favor.",
 "おねしゃす": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]",
 "おねだり": "تَسَوُّل (The act of one who begs.)  [begging]",
 "おねむ": "نَامَ, رَقَدَ (To rest in a state of reduced consciousness.) / نَوْم, سِنَة (The state of reduced consciousness during which a human or animal rests in a dai) / نَوْمَة (An act or instance of sleeping.) / غَمَص, رَمَص (Rheum, crusty or gummy discharge found in the corner of the eyes after waking, w)  [sleeping]",
 "おねんね": "نَامَ, رَقَدَ (To rest in a state of reduced consciousness.) / نَوْم, سِنَة (The state of reduced consciousness during which a human or animal rests in a dai) / نَوْمَة (An act or instance of sleeping.) / غَمَص, رَمَص (Rheum, crusty or gummy discharge found in the corner of the eyes after waking, w)  [sleeping]\nمثال: おねんねの時間よ。\n→ Time to go beddy-byes, dear. / حَبِيبِي (A person's romantic partner; a term of endearment used to refer to or address e.) / حَبِيبِي, عَزِيزِي (A form of address to a person considered to be attractive.)  [baby] / [childish person (esp. a young woman)]",
 "おの": "فَأْس (A tool for felling trees or chopping wood etc. consisting of a heavy head flatte)  [axe]\nمثال: 彼はおのでその木を切り倒した。\n→ He cut down the tree with an ax.",
