 "おめでたい": "سَعِيد (contented, joyous) / فَرِح (contented, joyous) / مَحْظُوظ (fortunate, lucky)  [happy (occasion, ending, etc.)]\nمثال: それ自体はおめでたいことですが、１つ気になるコメントがありました。\n→ This is a really good thing, but one comment keeps bothering me. / سَاذَج (Lacking worldly experience, wisdom, or judgement; unsophisticated.)  [naive]\nمثال: そんな話にだまされるなんて、よくよくおめでたいね。\n→ You must be very naive to be taken in by such a story.",
 "おめでたくなる": "مَاتَ (to stop living) / تُوُفِّيَ (to stop living) / زَهْر اَلطَّاوِلَة, زَهْر اَلنَّرْد (An isohedral polyhedron, usually a cube, with numbers or symbols on each side an)  [to die]\nused to avoid saying 死ぬ",
