 "お目にかかる": "لَاقَى, لَقِيَ (To make contact (with someone) while in proximity.) / اِلْتَقَى, تَقَابَلَ (To make contact (with someone) while in proximity.) / تَعَرَّفَ (To make contact (with someone) while in proximity.)  [to meet (someone of higher status)]\nمثال: 家内もお目にかかることを楽しみにしておりますから。\n→ My wife will be glad to see you, too. / [to be recognized (esp. by someone of higher status) ; to be visible]",
 "お目にかける": "ثَبَتَ, وَضَحَ (To display, convey or exhibit; to have something available for others to see; to) / عَرْض, اِسْتِعْرَاض (A play, dance, or other entertainment.) / بَرْنَامَج (A broadcast program, especially a light entertainment program.) / مَعْرِض (An agricultural exhibition.) / إِظْهَار, عَرْض (A demonstration.)  [to show]",
 "お目に掛かる": "لَاقَى, لَقِيَ (To make contact (with someone) while in proximity.) / اِلْتَقَى, تَقَابَلَ (To make contact (with someone) while in proximity.) / تَعَرَّفَ (To make contact (with someone) while in proximity.)  [to meet (someone of higher status)]\nمثال: 家内もお目にかかることを楽しみにしておりますから。\n→ My wife will be glad to see you, too. / [to be recognized (esp. by someone of higher status) ; to be visible]",
 "お目に掛ける": "ثَبَتَ, وَضَحَ (To display, convey or exhibit; to have something available for others to see; to) / عَرْض, اِسْتِعْرَاض (A play, dance, or other entertainment.) / بَرْنَامَج (A broadcast program, especially a light entertainment program.) / مَعْرِض (An agricultural exhibition.) / إِظْهَار, عَرْض (A demonstration.)  [to show]",
 "お目玉": "اِمْرَأَة سَلِيطَة (A person who habitually scolds, in particular a troublesome and angry woman.) / وَبَّخَ (To rebuke angrily.)  [scolding]",
 "お目目": "عَيْن, عين (An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).) / سُمّ, خُرْبَة (A hole at the blunt end of a needle through which thread is passed.)  [eyes]",
 "お目見え": "جُمْهُور, نَظَّارَة (A group of people within hearing; specifically, a large gathering of people list)  [audience (with a lord, dignitary, etc.)] / [first (public) appearance ; debut] / [trial service (of a servant) ; probation] / [audience with a shogun (granted to a vassal; Edo period) ; right to have an audience with a shogun]",
 "お目通り": "جُمْهُور, نَظَّارَة (A group of people within hearing; specifically, a large gathering of people list)  [audience (with someone of high standing)]",
 "お相子": "تَخَلَّى عَن, تَوَقَّفَ (To stop, give up (an activity).)  [quits]",
 "お眠": "نَامَ, رَقَدَ (To rest in a state of reduced consciousness.) / نَوْم, سِنَة (The state of reduced consciousness during which a human or animal rests in a dai) / نَوْمَة (An act or instance of sleeping.) / غَمَص, رَمَص (Rheum, crusty or gummy discharge found in the corner of the eyes after waking, w)  [sleeping]",
 "お知らせ": "لَاحَظَ (To remark upon; to mention.) / لَاحَظَ, اِنْتَبَهَ (To become aware of; to observe.)  [notice]\nمثال: 状況をお知らせください。\n→ Please let me know the status.",
 "お碗": "زِبْدِيَّة (container for food) / سُلْطَانِيَّة (container for food) / زُبْدِيَّة (container for food)  [bowl (ceramic, porcelain)]",
 "お礼": "شُكْرًا (Used to express appreciation or gratitude.)  [thanks]\nمثال: 息子に成り代わってお礼を申し上げます。\n→ I thank you on behalf of my son. / أُسْلُوب, طَرِيقَة (Mode of action; way of performing or doing anything.)  [manners] / قَوْس, قوس (A weapon made of a curved piece of wood or other flexible material whose ends ar) / اَنْشُوطَة, فيونكة (A type of knot with two loops, used to tie together two cords such as shoelaces ) / اِنْحَنَى (To play music on (a stringed) instrument using a bow.) / اِنْحَنَى لِلتَّحِيَّة, اِنْحَنَى (To bend oneself as a gesture of respect or deference.) / اِنْحِنَاءَة, اِلْتِوَاءَة (A gesture, usually showing respect, made by inclining the head or bending forwar) / قَيْدُوم (The front of a boat or ship.)  [bow] / مُكَافَأَة, ثَوَاب (Something of value given in return for an act.) / جَائِزَة (A prize promised for a certain deed or catch) / جَزَاء (The result of an action, whether good or bad.) / مَنَحَ (To give a reward to or for.)  [reward]",
 "お礼には及びません": "عَفْوًا (A polite way of responding to thanks, by suggesting that the service is too triv)  [don't mention it]",
 "お祈り": "صَلَاة, دُعَاء (A practice of communicating with one's God, or with some spiritual entity.) / صَلَاة (An act of praying.) / صَلَاة (The specific words or methods used for praying.) / مُصَلٍّ (One who prays.)  [prayer]\nمثال: ご成功をお祈りします。\n→ I wish you every success.",
 "お祓い": "تَطْهِير (The act or process of purifying; the removal of impurities.)  [purification]",
 "お祖母さん": "جَدَّة (A mother of someone's parent.)  [grandmother]\nusu. お祖母さん when written with kanji\nمثال: ジョンのおばあさんは長い間病に伏せていたが、亡くなった。\n→ John's grandmother passed away after a long illness. / عَجُوز (An elderly woman.)  [old woman]\nusu. お婆さん when written with kanji\nمثال: お祖母さんが座布団の上にちんまりとすわっていました。\n→ The old woman was snugly sitting on a cushion.",
 "お祖母ちゃま": "جَدَّة, تِيتَة (Grandmother.)  [grandma]",
 "お祖母様": "جَدَّة (A mother of someone's parent.)  [grandmother]\nusu. お祖母様 when written with kanji / عَجُوز (An elderly woman.)  [old woman]\nusu. お婆様 when written with kanji",
 "お祖父さん": "جَدّ (The archived older version of a file that immediately preceded the father file.)  [grandfather]\nusu. お祖父さん when written with kanji\nمثال: おじいさんは少し耳が遠いんだ。\n→ My grandfather is a bit hard of hearing. / شَيْخ, عَجُوز (An elderly man.)  [old man]\nusu. お爺さん when written with kanji\nمثال: おじいさんはその木の人形をピノキオと名づけました。\n→ The old man named the wooden doll Pinocchio.",
 "お祖父ちゃま": "جَدِّي (grandfather.)  [grandpa]",
 "お祖父様": "جَدّ (The archived older version of a file that immediately preceded the father file.)  [grandfather]\nusual kanji form is お祖父様 / شَيْخ, عَجُوز (An elderly man.)  [old man]\nusual kanji form is お爺様",
 "お祝": "تَهْنِئَة (The act of congratulating.)  [congratulation] / حَالِيّ, حَاضِر (Relating to now, for the time being; current.) / مَوْجُود, حَاضِر (Located in the immediate vicinity.) / الزَّمَان, الْحَال (The current moment or period of time.) / قَدَّمَ, طَرَحَ (To bring (someone) into the presence of (a person); to introduce formally.)  [present]",
