 "お願いだから": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: お願いだから泣かないで。\n→ Please don't cry.",
 "お願い事": "طَلَبَ (to express the need or desire for) / طَلَب, مَسْأَلَة (Act of requesting (with the adposition at in the presence of possessives, and on)  [request]\nمثال: あなたにお願い事をしてもよいでしょうか。\n→ Can I ask you a favor?",
 "お願い申し上げる": "سَأَلَ, سأل (To request or petition.)  [to ask (humbly)]\nمثال: 浅学非才の私ではありますが、何とぞ皆様のお力を賜りたく、ここにお願い申し上げる次第です。\n→ I may not have much to offer in the way of learning or ability, but I want to do whatever I can for us all and humbly ask for your favor.",
 "お願い致します": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: お願いいたします、最後までお聞きください。\n→ I do beseech you, hear me through.",
 "お風呂": "حَمَّام, مُغْسَل (A tub or pool which is used for bathing: bathtub.) / حَمَّام, مُغْتَسَل (A building or area where bathing occurs.) / اِسْتِحْمَام, اِغْتِسَال (The act of bathing; an instance of this; the taking of a bath.)  [bath]\nمثال: 私はほとんど毎日お風呂に入ります。\n→ I take a bath almost every day.",
